WEBVTT

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.720
So cold.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:14.990
Mary.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.820
Morning.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.420
Good morning.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.410
What? What do you want?

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.790
I was just saying hi.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.050
I see.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.720
Hey, um...

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.830
Is Shun-chan going to...

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.730
be eating lunch in the cafeteria today?

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:39.690
Yeah.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.490
Really?

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:42.370
Okay, see you later.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:48.800
Chizuru.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.260
What are you doing by the 
first years' lockers?

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:56.680
Yuta, let him be.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.670
He's finally found the will to 
start over again from first year.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.200
I see.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.750
That's not it!

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.040
That's so good.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.300
Nothing beats a hot bowl of udon in the winter.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.530
Right?

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:41.780
Kaname, can't you look a little
happier when you're eating?

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.150
You're making my food taste bad.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.540
Shut up.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.830
Whose fault is it that I'm eating 
convenience store bread?

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.780
Don't ruin the bag, Kaname.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.650
I haven't taken the sticker off yet.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.750
How many more stickers do you need?

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.740
A lot more.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:09.160
It's your fault for coming up 
with this "sticker duty" thing, monkey.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.330
Kanamecchi, I know you're upset because...

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.910
you don't get to eat your 
mother's homemade lunch,

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.540
but don't take it out on us.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.120
That's got nothing to do with this!

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.350
Try to keep it down in 
the cafeteria, you two.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:21.050
Shun-chan.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.430
Masaki-chan.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.020
Have you finished eating?

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:26.920
Yes.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.220
What did you do to your finger?

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:32.150
It's nothing.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.010
Anyway...

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.380
I wanted to show you this.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.950
That's the bear I gave you.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.740
But, those clothes...

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.950
I tried making him an outfit.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.210
That's amazing, Masaki-chan.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.320
Can I take a look?

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.250
Sure.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.680
Huh? Mary did this?

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:55.610
H-Hey, what do you think you're doing?

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:56.340
Ow.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.420
I was just looking at his pants.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.800
I can't help but get the feeling...

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.190
that you're looking for something 
when you turn up his pants.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:07.120
Santa doesn't keep adult 
presents in there.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.100
I know that!

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.110
Sheesh.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.490
I'm sure the bear loves his new clothes.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:15.020
That's good.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:21.690
Even though no one beckons it,

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.990
the winter dutifully arrives every year.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:28.270
Today's another cold winter's day.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:33.520
That concludes today's Student Council meeting.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.810
Ugh. It's still raining?

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.480
What am I going to do?

00:04:59.060 --> 00:04:59.930
Hey.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:02.480
What are you up to, Shorty?

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.750
Don't go stealing someone 
else's umbrella.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.300
Y-You're wrong! It's the other way around!

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.240
Someone stole my umbrella!

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.400
You have my sympathies.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.140
Umbrellas get stolen 
at school all the time.

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:18.500
Your home's in the same direction as mine, isn't it?

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.500
Do you want to share mine?

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.510
It's fine. Besides, I'm sure you'd...

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.670
You'd probably hog the umbrella, anyway.

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:29.760
Like hell I would!

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.240
Fine, fine.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.890
Have fun getting wet, then.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.030
Bye.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.190
H-Hey, wait! What are you doing?

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:48.810
Oh, come on.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:50.270
It's true.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.250
Whoa, hold up.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.950
Isn't that Sato-san?

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:00.910
What?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.340
You can't be serious.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.000
She's sharing an umbrella with a boy.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.570
Who is she with?

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.870
Isn't that guy on the Student Council?

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.130
What?

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.260
No way. Why?

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.200
Good morning.

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:27.560
Did you hear?

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:29.890
She's with an upperclassman 
who's on the Student Council.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:32.320
What? Oh, that?

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.220
Good morning, Sato-san.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:42.900
D-Do you mind if I ask 
you a weird question?

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:48.470
Sato-san, are you going 
out with Tsukahara-senpai?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.070
My friend told me that...

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.430
she saw you guys sharing an umbrella yesterday,

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.680
and that you kissed.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.480
Of course we didn't!

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:02.530
You'd have to be crazy to think 
I'd do something like that!

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.820
There's no way that would ever happen!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.820
His upper limit's Kaori-sensei, 
his lower limit's Masaki.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:12.060
Your playing field's too wide, Senpai.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.330
I don't even know where the line in the sand is.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.830
Who are you calling "Senpai"?

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:16.620
Are you stupid?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.800
I-It didn't happen! 
It didn't happen, Shun-chan!

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:23.510
I didn't want to go, 
but Kaname forced me to...

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:23.510
You forced her?

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:26.050
Does that make you a 
dangerous individual,

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.250
like a street slasher?

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:30.910
Shorty, stop saying things that'll 
give them the wrong idea!

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:31.510
Listen up!

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:34.040
She said she had something in her eye,

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.850
so I just leaned down to check!

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:40.290
Okay, okay. Everyone 
makes up their own excuses.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.570
It's not an excuse!

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.610
You're dead!

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.280
You have some gall to think...

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:49.450
you'd getting away with kissing Mary!

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:53.120
You're not Kanamecchi any 
more, you're <i>Kana-messed up</i>!

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.570
Won't any of you listen to me?!

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:56.310
This mouth?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:08:00.450
Is this the mouth you used to kiss Mary?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.490
What do you think you're doing?

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.240
Homeroom's about to—

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:10.290
Huh?

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.890
I heard you were dating Sato-san, but...

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.000
I see.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.850
You're wrong on both counts!

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:25.290
I can't believe I got so carried away.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:26.500
Now that I think about it,

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.150
there's no way you'd go for Mary.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.800
Kanamecchi, you already have 
your mom and Kaori-sensei.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.190
No, I don't.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.600
I suppose I'll make an exception,

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.550
and forgive you for sharing an umbrella.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:42.000
Chizuru-san, exceptions don't 
really count as forgiving.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.100
This is ridiculous.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:48.190
Now, now. Winter vacation's coming up.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:51.090
I'm sure the rumors will 
disappear over the break.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.550
Right?

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.220
Chizuru, why do you seem so happy?

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:59.120
Hey, Christmas isn't long after 
the beginning of the break.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.600
Let's all do something on Christmas.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.580
What? But it's cold then.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:07.240
Hey! Don't be so glum!

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:10.270
The city's already alive 
with the sound of jingle bells!

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.870
I'll just stay at home, then.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:16.980
You take a nap, and by the time 
you wake up, Christmas is already over.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:20.060
Your lives as young men are over.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:21.890
What's wrong with you?

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.600
Why won't you hang out with us?

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:26.500
It's not like...

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:30.460
It's not like any of us have girlfriends!

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.910
Someone hold me all night!

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:35.350
You don't have to shout it!

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.150
<i>Damn it. They're all so cold.</i>

00:09:55.810 --> 00:10:01.050
<i>If I had a girlfriend, I would 
have a present or two.</i>

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.240
This is so cute.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.200
It so is.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.580
I bet you'd look good in this.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.210
Maybe I'll get it.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:17.470
Is this really what girls like?

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:22.960
I bet this would look good on Mary.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.620
Oh, man. She's too cute.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:32.770
Really? You'll buy this for me?

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.420
Sure. It's almost Christmas.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.530
I'm so happy. Thank you.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.670
No, no, no. No way.

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:50.780
I could never get her a present.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:53.340
I know it's Christmas, but there's 
no way it would go that well.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:57.170
Look at this. This hair ribbon is so cute.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.700
You're right.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:02.970
Huh?

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.140
<i>I-I bought it.</i>

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.620
<i>Maybe I made a mistake.</i>

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:13.260
<i>Yeah, but... but...</i>

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.530
Spots... Stripes...

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:29.820
Spots... Stripes...

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.080
Spots...

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:33.630
Stripes.

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:34.790
Spots.

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.810
Hey. Are you shopping too, Mary?

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:38.820
What a coincidence.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:42.210
Don't "hey" me. You scared me.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.800
I-Is Shun-chan with you?

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.930
No, I'm here by myself.

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:51.230
I see.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:58.320
That'll be 525 yen.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.360
Oh, um...

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.460
Could you gift wrap it, please?

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:06.810
Very well.

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:15.790
Hey, Mary.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.780
This is just a guess,

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:21.220
but that's not a Christmas present 
for Shun-chan, is it?

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.820
A girl giving a guy a present?

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:27.300
Don't you think that's a little weird?

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.210
I-It's not weird.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:31.880
It's not a Christmas present.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:34.900
He gave me the bear keychain 
at the summer festival,

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.980
and he's always helping 
me with my studies.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.910
I-It's to thank him!

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.610
So, it's fine if I give this to him!

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.030
Fine, fine.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:44.210
That's a stretch.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.760
What the heck?

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:14.220
It's been raining so much lately.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:17.770
It's December. Where's the snow?

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:20.130
What am I going to do?

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.280
I didn't bring an umbrella.

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:29.340
You shouldn't do that.

00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:32.520
Just so you know, I don't 
have a handkerchief.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:37.830
I never expected you to have one.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.680
Wait, what kind of impression do you have of me?

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:43.990
That sort of impression.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:45.050
I see.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:17.570
Mary, this...

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:19.020
You two.

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:20.600
Yes?

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:22.490
You make a cute couple.

00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:25.410
No! We're not a couple!

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.410
I only have one umbrella,

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:26.630
but would you like to use it?

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:28.770
Really? Are you sure?

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:31.160
Thank you, then.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:35.520
Is that what we look like?

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.090
Looks like there are still 
some nice people in the world.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:41.860
<i>Sharing an umbrella.</i>

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.570
Come on. Get under.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:47.490
Mary?

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:51.490
I'm fine.

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:56.790
You're fine? You're not getting under it?

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:59.180
But she gave us this—

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:02.540
If someone starts another weird rumor,

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:05.500
Shun-chan will get the wrong idea again.

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:12.710
With Kanamecchi, people saw you...

00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:15.300
because you were near the school.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:18.310
We're pretty far from the school here,

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.620
so it'll be fine.

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:21.850
Here, come on.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:31.860
You don't need to be so 
worried about rumors, anyway.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.310
Shun-chan won't care either way.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:41.840
W-Wait, that's not what I mean. I just...

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:45.230
Mary, wait!

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:46.300
Take the umbrella.

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:15.820
How many more days until spring break?

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:21.000
Chizuru-san, you've just 
skipped an entire season.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.180
I've had enough of winter.

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:26.380
My body and soul are plenty cold already.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:29.630
It hasn't even snowed yet this year.

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.170
Oh, right.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.200
All the hot couples of the world...

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:36.550
are accelerating global warming.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:39.180
Love's supposed to save the world,

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:41.600
so I'm not sure that's it.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:43.610
What's wrong with you?

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:45.770
Winter vacation starts tomorrow.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:48.150
What happened to your Christmas cheer?

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:55.050
Oh, it's Masaki.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:00.860
Shorty.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:03.960
What are you doing?

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.330
I-I didn't see Shun-chan in Class 5,

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.430
so I thought he might be here.

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:10.340
Shun? He's not here.

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:14.940
Is that a Christmas present for Shun?

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:15.960
Of course.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:18.010
Today's your last chance 
to give this to him.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:19.020
Hey, it's none of your business! Give it back!

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.140
Lucky you, Tsukahara.

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:23.290
Is that a Christmas present 
from your little girlfriend?

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.870
What? She's not my girlfriend.

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:27.270
What'd she give you? Let's see.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.650
You idiot, that's not for me.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:32.180
You shouldn't take people's presents...

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:34.130
just because you're jealous.

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.930
Get out of here.

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:37.240
What's wrong with you?

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:39.520
You're not curious, Tachibana?

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:45.490
Here.

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:48.580
The ribbon's just a little crooked.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:50.800
Nothing's wrong with the present inside.

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:55.610
Okay.

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:07.900
Welcome back.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.280
What did Masaki want?

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:14.110
The lights are on.

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:15.880
It's beautiful.

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:18.730
You guys really like that 
kind of thing, don't you?

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:21.570
Who cares about some stupid decoration?

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:24.410
Shut up. Boys wouldn't get it.

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:28.870
These cute decorations give us a buzz.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:51.450
Mary!

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:03.990
Why are you going home?

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:07.930
Wh-Who are you?

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:11.280
Who am I? I'm Chizuru.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:13.270
Why are you going home?

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:15.460
What about your present to Shun-chan?

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:20.130
You haven't given it to him.

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:24.720
But the ribbon's all messed up.

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:43.200
Here.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.540
Now it's all good.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.330
Come on, come on.

00:19:58.330 --> 00:19:59.510
Go, go, go.

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:01.460
Go on. Go on.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.110
Stop it, you pervert.

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:43.790
So cold.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:58.540
I gave it to him.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:01.780
What'd he say?

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:03.830
"Thanks."

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:07.070
That's great.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:16.380
Hey...

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:24.840
What are you doing?

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:33.180
Here, I got it.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.280
Oh, sorry.

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:36.130
Thanks...

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:44.320
for the ribbon.

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:48.330
If you...

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:54.260
don't have an umbrella, 
you can share mine.

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:59.340
If you have your own...

00:22:00.050 --> 00:22:01.460
N-No! I don't!

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:04.820
I totally didn't bring one today!

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:06.230
Just wait here! My bag!

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:08.430
I'll go get my bag, so wait here!

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:10.180
Don't leave!

00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:23.130
All right!

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:26.870
Viva Christmas!

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:29.860
Hurry up and get here, my spring.

00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:33.700
But just for now, stop right here.

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:35.490
My winter with you.

00:24:15.840 --> 00:24:18.630
The next episode is "Very Christmas."
